{{- define "pr-context-description" -}}
## Input Context

You will receive a PRContext containing:

- `owner`, `repo`, `number`: Repository and PR identifiers
- `title`, `body`: PR title and description
- `base_ref`, `head_ref`, `head_sha`: Branch information
- `user_login`: PR author
- `labels`, `assignees`: PR metadata
- `changed_files`: Array of file changes with:
  - `path`: File path
  - `status`: added/modified/removed/renamed
  - `patch`: Unified diff (when `include_patch=true`)
  - `contents_b64`: Base64-encoded file contents (when `include_file_contents=true`)
- `guidelines_b64`: Base64-encoded review guidelines (from CLAUDE.md or similar)
- `extra_files`: Additional repository files
- `triggered_by`: User who triggered the review
- `event_name`: `pull_request` or `issue_comment`
- `trigger_text`: Comment body for mention-triggered runs
- `prompt_text`: Rendered prompt template (if configured)
{{- end -}}
